usage_214988060991_module_2_0_0_2,214988060991,CP W20 — Newsletter Maintenance Tips,AUTOMATED_DRAFT,AUTOMATED_EMAIL,all_emails_recheck.json,,snapshot,draft_snapshot_if_source_was_draft_else_export_snapshot,@hubspot/email/ecommerce/ecommerce_abandoned_cart_4.html,builtin_hubspot_image_email,builtin_hubspot,HubSpot built-in modules,@hubspot/image_email,,module-2-0-0,,,,section-2,2,0,0,,"{""css_class"":""dnd-module"",""hs_enable_module_padding"":true,""hs_wrapper_css"":{""padding-bottom"":""20px"",""padding-left"":""20px"",""padding-right"":""20px"",""padding-top"":""20px""},""img"":{""alt"":""Close-up of a fresh haircut and style at the barber"",""height"":320,""loading"":""disabled"",""src"":""https://res.cloudinary.com/dtmizxj1n/image/upload/w_600,h_300,c_fill,g_auto,q_auto,f_auto/v1/fresh-style-close-up-barber"",""width"":560},""lineNumber"":61,""link"":""https://hairsolutions.co/collections/maintenance"",""parent_widget_container"":null,""schema_version"":2,""startPosition"":-1015}",7355b42d4ceb7d52d1c4b1c1e748145e2cc71e9e9ae8d9fb8d740016118a9245,False,True,2026-07-03,observed_in_hubspot_json,legacy_builtin_or_native_hubspot_module,
usage_214988060991_module_3_0_0_3,214988060991,CP W20 — Newsletter Maintenance Tips,AUTOMATED_DRAFT,AUTOMATED_EMAIL,all_emails_recheck.json,,snapshot,draft_snapshot_if_source_was_draft_else_export_snapshot,@hubspot/email/ecommerce/ecommerce_abandoned_cart_4.html,builtin_hubspot_rich_text,builtin_hubspot,HubSpot built-in modules,@hubspot/rich_text,,module-3-0-0,,,,section-3,3,0,0,,"{""css_class"":""dnd-module"",""hs_enable_module_padding"":true,""hs_wrapper_css"":{""padding-bottom"":""20px"",""padding-left"":""40px"",""padding-right"":""40px"",""padding-top"":""16px""},""html"":""<div style=\""font-family:Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:150%;color:#1A1A1A;\""><p style=\""margin:0 0 16px 0;font-family:Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:150%;font-weight:400;color:#1A1A1A;\""><strong>Top 5 Maintenance Mistakes (and How to Fix Them)</strong></p><p style=\""margin:0 0 16px 0;font-family:Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:150%;font-weight:400;color:#1A1A1A;\"">After thousands of customer conversations, the same mistakes keep coming up. Here are the five that shorten system life and weaken bonds the most:</p><p style=\""margin:0 0 16px 0;font-family:Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:150%;font-weight:400;color:#1A1A1A;\""><strong>1. Skipping scalp prep.</strong> Applying adhesive over residue or oils is the number one reason bonds fail early. Every attachment should start with a clean, dry scalp. <strong>2. Using too much adhesive.</strong> More glue does not mean a stronger bond. It means a messier removal and more residue buildup. Thin, even coats are always better. <strong>3. Ignoring the perimeter.</strong> The edges of your system take the most stress. If you are not pressing and sealing the perimeter after every wash, you are inviting lift. <strong>4. Washing with the wrong products.</strong> Sulfate-heavy shampoos strip the hair and degrade adhesive bonds. Switch to a sulfate-free, system-safe shampoo. <strong>5. Waiting too long between maintenance.</strong> Regular 2-3 week maintenance cycles keep your system looking fresh and your scalp healthy. Stretching it to 4-5 weeks causes buildup and reduces the life of the unit.</p><p style=\""margin:0 0 16px 0;font-family:Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:150%;font-weight:400;color:#1A1A1A;\""><strong>Seasonal Care Note:</strong> As we move into warmer months, increase your wash frequency slightly and consider switching to a water-based adhesive if you are not already using one. Heat and humidity break down solvent-based glues faster.</p><p style=\""margin:0 0 16px 0;font-family:Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:150%;font-weight:400;color:#1A1A1A;\""><strong>Restocking Reminder:</strong> If you are running low on adhesive, remover, or scalp cleanser, now is the time to restock before summer. Our maintenance bundles save you 15% compared to buying individual products.</p><p style=\""margin:0 0 16px 0;font-family:Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:150%;font-weight:400;color:#1A1A1A;\""><strong>Product Spotlight:</strong> Our new Scalp Refresh Spray is designed for mid-cycle freshness — spray it along the perimeter to clean and re-seal without a full removal. It has quickly become one of our best sellers.</p></div>"",""lineNumber"":94,""parent_widget_container"":null,""schema_version"":2,""startPosition"":-442}",2fa8223d84875f6f4b8d01b25db15083a1be0ee696ad91f4cb5fb0f4f6ebc6cb,False,True,2026-07-03,observed_in_hubspot_json,legacy_builtin_or_native_hubspot_module,
