usage_214988406444_module_1_0_0_1,214988406444,CP W22 — Color Matching Education,AUTOMATED_DRAFT,AUTOMATED_EMAIL,all_emails_recheck.json,,snapshot,draft_snapshot_if_source_was_draft_else_export_snapshot,@hubspot/email/ecommerce/ecommerce_abandoned_cart_4.html,builtin_hubspot_rich_text,builtin_hubspot,HubSpot built-in modules,@hubspot/rich_text,,module-1-0-0,,,,section-1,1,0,0,,"{""css_class"":""dnd-module"",""hs_enable_module_padding"":true,""hs_wrapper_css"":{""padding-bottom"":""28px"",""padding-left"":""40px"",""padding-right"":""40px"",""padding-top"":""16px""},""html"":""<div style=\""font-family:Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:150%;color:#FFFFFF;\""><h1 style=\""margin:0;font-family:Arial Black,Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:52px;line-height:108%;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-0.3px;text-align:center;color:#FFFFFF;\"">COLOR MATCHING, DECODED.</h1><p style=\""margin:16px 0 0 0;font-family:Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:150%;font-weight:400;text-align:center;color:#FFFFFF;\"">Color codes, gray blending, and samples explained.</p></div>"",""lineNumber"":94,""parent_widget_container"":null,""schema_version"":2,""startPosition"":-442}",735a43febbf7821c273941f06d9a564bfd17e48cc7dba8ba6b561d74880693b6,False,True,2026-07-03,observed_in_hubspot_json,legacy_builtin_or_native_hubspot_module,
usage_214988406444_module_2_0_0_2,214988406444,CP W22 — Color Matching Education,AUTOMATED_DRAFT,AUTOMATED_EMAIL,all_emails_recheck.json,,snapshot,draft_snapshot_if_source_was_draft_else_export_snapshot,@hubspot/email/ecommerce/ecommerce_abandoned_cart_4.html,builtin_hubspot_image_email,builtin_hubspot,HubSpot built-in modules,@hubspot/image_email,,module-2-0-0,,,,section-2,2,0,0,,"{""css_class"":""dnd-module"",""hs_enable_module_padding"":true,""hs_wrapper_css"":{""padding-bottom"":""20px"",""padding-left"":""20px"",""padding-right"":""20px"",""padding-top"":""20px""},""img"":{""alt"":""Hair coloring and matching at a salon (temporary — GAP-04 needs AI generation)"",""height"":320,""loading"":""disabled"",""src"":""https://res.cloudinary.com/dtmizxj1n/image/upload/w_600,h_300,c_fill,g_auto,q_auto,f_auto/v1/hair-coloring-salon"",""width"":560},""lineNumber"":61,""link"":""https://hairsolutions.co/pages/color-guide"",""parent_widget_container"":null,""schema_version"":2,""startPosition"":-1015}",b9da231b969fddd9d86732402249ed0bab96db2ce911fb148b5df729bb749508,False,True,2026-07-03,observed_in_hubspot_json,legacy_builtin_or_native_hubspot_module,
usage_214988406444_module_3_0_0_3,214988406444,CP W22 — Color Matching Education,AUTOMATED_DRAFT,AUTOMATED_EMAIL,all_emails_recheck.json,,snapshot,draft_snapshot_if_source_was_draft_else_export_snapshot,@hubspot/email/ecommerce/ecommerce_abandoned_cart_4.html,builtin_hubspot_rich_text,builtin_hubspot,HubSpot built-in modules,@hubspot/rich_text,,module-3-0-0,,,,section-3,3,0,0,,"{""css_class"":""dnd-module"",""hs_enable_module_padding"":true,""hs_wrapper_css"":{""padding-bottom"":""20px"",""padding-left"":""40px"",""padding-right"":""40px"",""padding-top"":""16px""},""html"":""<div style=\""font-family:Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:150%;color:#1A1A1A;\""><p style=\""margin:0 0 16px 0;font-family:Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:150%;font-weight:400;color:#1A1A1A;\"">Getting the right color is just as important as getting the right base — and it is the area where most first-time buyers feel the least confident. Hair system color charts can look overwhelming, but once you understand the logic behind them, choosing becomes straightforward.</p><p style=\""margin:0 0 16px 0;font-family:Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:150%;font-weight:400;color:#1A1A1A;\""><strong>Understanding Color Codes:</strong> Most hair system colors use a numbering system. #1 is jet black, #1B is off-black, #2 is darkest brown, and the numbers go up through medium brown (#4), light brown (#6), dark blonde (#8), and beyond. The key is that these numbers are standardized across the industry, so you can compare confidently. If you currently wear a #4 from any brand, a #4 from us will be in the same family.</p><p style=\""margin:0 0 16px 0;font-family:Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:150%;font-weight:400;color:#1A1A1A;\""><strong>Gray Percentage:</strong> This is where customization gets powerful. If you have natural graying, we can blend gray into your system at any percentage — 5%, 10%, 20%, all the way up. Matching your natural gray level is what makes a system look age- appropriate and completely undetectable. Our recommendation: aim for slightly less gray than your natural hair, since systems do not gray over time the way natural hair does.</p><p style=\""margin:0 0 16px 0;font-family:Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:150%;font-weight:400;color:#1A1A1A;\""><strong>Hair Density:</strong> Density refers to how thick the hair is across the system. Light, medium-light, medium, and medium-heavy are the standard options. Most men do best with medium-light to medium — it looks the most natural. Going too heavy is the most common mistake. A natural-looking density always beats a thick, obviously full head of hair.</p><p style=\""margin:0 0 16px 0;font-family:Helvetica Neue,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:150%;font-weight:400;color:#1A1A1A;\""><strong>Order a Sample:</strong> If this is your first order or you are switching colors, we strongly recommend ordering a color sample ring. It ships free, arrives in 2-3 days, and lets you match against your natural hair in your own lighting. It takes the guesswork out entirely.</p></div>"",""lineNumber"":94,""parent_widget_container"":null,""schema_version"":2,""startPosition"":-442}",f4321fc9ccc285e0d70456241d77a6513f9094984c24714539ca921fb70e532c,False,True,2026-07-03,observed_in_hubspot_json,legacy_builtin_or_native_hubspot_module,
